    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Dollar Shave Club started with one video that cost about $4,500.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.55,
        "window": 4.23,
        "fill": 0.839
      },
      {
        "scene": "funded",
        "text": "The day it went up, investors put in $1M. Then the orders poured in.",
        "start": 4.53,
        "seconds": 3.5,
        "window": 4.13,
        "fill": 0.847
      },
      {
        "scene": "bet",
        "text": "Its bet: razor blades mailed to your door every month, instead of a trip to the shop. Would anyone sign up?",
        "start": 8.67,
        "seconds": 4.42,
        "window": 5.07,
        "fill": 0.872
      },
      {
        "scene": "growth",
        "text": "The founder told Fortune it sold $4M in its first year, $19M the next, then $65M.",
        "start": 13.73,
        "seconds": 5.95,
        "window": 6.63,
        "fill": 0.897
      },
      {
        "scene": "question",
        "text": "So what is a box of mailed razors really worth?",
        "start": 20.37,
        "seconds": 1.73,
        "window": 2.33,
        "fill": 0.742
      },
      {
        "scene": "turn",
        "text": "Four years after that video, Unilever, the company behind Dove soap, came to buy it.",
        "start": 22.7,
        "seconds": 3.41,
        "window": 4.0,
        "fill": 0.853
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "Fortune's sources put the price at $1B, all in cash, for a company one cheap video started.",
        "start": 26.7,
        "seconds": 4.74,
        "window": 5.4,
        "fill": 0.878
      },
      {
        "scene": "ending",
        "text": "Mailed blades or the shop shelf: where do you buy yours? Either way, it all goes back to one video.",
        "start": 32.1,
        "seconds": 4.32,
        "window": 4.97,
